cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results, please cite the paper and this artifact."
title: "Class-Level Data Efficiency in Industrial Defect Classification: results, splits, and analysis pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Complete experimental artifact for a study of class-level data efficiency in
  industrial surface-defect classification. Contains 6,430 completed training
  runs (2,700 main benchmark + 3,730 pilot sweep) over four public industrial
  defect datasets, eleven torchvision classifiers, and per-class annotation-budget
  sweeps with five seeds. Each run records its per-class accuracy and full
  confusion matrix. Also includes the frozen data splits, the dataset audit
  records, the aggregated analysis tables, and the code that regenerates every
  table and figure in the manuscript.
